---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, href } from "../data/site";
---
<Base title="About" description="What the orchestra is, the crops and decisions it serves, and the two rules that make its results safe to act on." path="/about">
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>R packages for crop decisions based on cause and effect</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">Scientific analysis increasingly feeds a fitted model straight into an automated
        decision, and the risk is easy to miss: a model that fits an outcome well can still rest on an
        association that is driven by some third factor, or that nobody has checked, and a pipeline that
        simply tunes a model and then optimises against it will act on that association.</p>
      <p class="mt-2"><strong>Withholding a result</strong>: the system gives no recommendation when the
        evidence is too thin to detect the effect, when the different methods applied to the same question
        disagree, or when an input has not been checked, and it records why. <strong>The independent-check
        rule</strong>: facts about outside sources are checked against a reference the orchestra did not
        produce, and unchecked inputs are not used (set out in full under
        <a href={href("/governance")}>Governance</a>). Every package writes its results in the same versioned
        record, the manifest, and an engine runs the analysis plan, checking at each step that the result
        passed on is the kind the next step expects.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">Domain</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">{site.domain}. Every method must be shown working on a real grain-production
        decision; a method that cannot be is set aside, not pursued. All data used are data that can be
        published (public agricultural trial datasets and crop simulators); no restricted field data
        enters any package.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">How this site was checked</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">Every package name, description and count on this site was checked against the
        packages' own DESCRIPTION files and the DataHub catalogue on 1 October 2026.</p>

      <p class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/members")}>The packages</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/")}>Home</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
